# GINVIFY CAT — MASCOT RULES

Applies to anything under `components/mascot/`. See spec Section 5B.

## What it is

- A minimal, geometric, line-art cute cat — built from the same visual
  vocabulary as the Intelligence Core (thin outlines, small circular "node"
  joints at ears/paws/tail tip, optional soft glow in `#B7FF3C` or
  `#5CE1E6` on hover / in dark sections).
- Not a cartoon character, not a plush illustration, not a "SaaS mascot."
  No separate cartoon color palette — stay within the site's near-black +
  accent-color system.
- No dialogue, no personality-driven copy, no jokes. It's a quiet visual
  signature, not a brand character with a voice.

## Where it is allowed to appear (exhaustive list)

- 404 / error page.
- Empty states (e.g. empty filtered results in Experiments, empty
  contact-form confirmation state).
- A small, unobtrusive footer easter egg near the language switch or
  copyright line.
- Optional lightweight loading indicator on non-critical pages only.

## Where it must NEVER appear

- Hero.
- Main scroll story (Idea → Architecture → Intelligence → Software →
  Automation → Scale).
- Services, AI, Automation, Engineering, Technology sections.
- Navigation or as the primary logo (the primary logo is the static G
  logotype — the particle version of the G is reserved for the 3D
  experience only).

## Implementation

- Single reusable component: `GinvifyCat.tsx`, SVG line-art, a few
  animation variants (idle, blink, tail-flick, wave for empty states).
- Provide a static fallback pose for `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Meaningful alt text / accessible description required wherever it's used
  — never a decoration-only image with no semantic fallback.
- Keep this component's imports isolated: it should never be imported into
  any file under `components/three/` or the homepage scroll-story sections.
  If you find yourself doing that, stop — it's out of scope for where the
  mascot belongs.
